00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:27,560
 Now let's say you're a flight booking agent and the user has given you details on booking

73
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:31,720
 a flight from New York to Chicago on a particular date.

74
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:37,800
 But as an agent, you found multiple flights, one that's a direct flight and then one flight,

75
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:39,000
 which is one stop.

76
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:43,280
 And the user has not provided whether he wants a direct flight or one stop flight.

77
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:48,240
 So in that case, if you enable this, then the agent can go ahead and ask a clarifying

78
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:50,920
 question to the end user.

79
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:55,680
 And if you keep it disabled, then it will just make an assumption and go ahead and process

80
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:57,920
 that request.

81
00:05:57,920 --> 00:05:59,640
 Next you have the KMS.

82
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:05,360
 So if you want to encrypt your data, you can use the KMS service.

83
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:07,040
 Next you have the idle session timeout.

84
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:09,720
 So this is mainly the short term memory of the agent.

85
00:06:09,720 --> 00:06:15,600
 So you can determine the duration for which you need to keep the session active between

86
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:18,600
