00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:33,160
 and coordinates a response by default, orchestration is defined by advanced prompts that can

163
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:36,720
 be overridden or customized for advanced use case.

164
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:42,160
 So you can either use default orchestration prompts based on the large language model that

165
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:44,560
 you have selected or you can write your own.

166
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:50,680
 So we just click on this edit and you can see these orchestration templates here.

167
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:56,640
 So you can see for pre-processing, orchestration, knowledge base and then you have one more

168
00:11:56,640 --> 00:12:02,040
 post-processing and if you just click on this orchestration, we have the override orchestration

169
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:03,400
 template defaults.

170
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:08,000
 So you can override and write your own, but we just go to the continue with the default

171
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:12,080
 ones and here prompt template editor.

172
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:17,720
 So these are some of the instructions that are sent to the large language model along

173
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:21,600
 with the user query and if you see here.

174
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:28,360
 So it's telling the large language model on how to process the user input and here you

175
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:34,240
 can see it says in the thought first answer the following question, what is the user's goal?

176
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:36,360
 What information has just been provided?

177
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:42,880
 What is the best action plan or step by step action to fulfill the user's request?

178
00:12:42,880 --> 00:12:44,560
 So how does this help?

179
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:52,600
 It basically helps in chain of thought and reasoning and action planning step for the agent.

180
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:59,480
 So let's say the user has sent a query, book up flight for me with following detail.

181
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:04,840
 So what the large language model driving the agent is going to do is it's going to break

182
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:08,200
 down that user tasks into these seven steps.

183
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:10,760
 So what's the user goal to book a flight?

184
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:12,760
 What information has been provided?

185
00:13:12,760 --> 00:13:16,800
 So he's providing me the name, date, source, destination.

186
00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:18,160
 What is the best action plan?

187
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:24,320
 So it will break down that user request into multiple steps that didn't take maybe make

188
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:27,680
 a call to the airline booking database and so on.

189
00:13:27,680 --> 00:13:30,800
 So this is what an orchestration prompt does.

190
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:33,240
 Similarly, you have one for the knowledge base.

191
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:38,320
 So if there is a request related to the knowledge basis, how that is going to be executed

192
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:45,680
 and then you have the post processing, which defines how the agent determined the final

193
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:47,240
 response.

194
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:53,800
 So if we just click on cancel and then finally we have the multi agent collaboration.

195
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:58,960
 So when we want to have multiple agents as part of a application, then you will use this

196
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,440
 multi agent collaboration.

197
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:02,640
 So if we just click on this edit.

198
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:05,120
 So here it shows collaboration status.

199
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:10,840
 So if I just enable this multi agent collaboration, then first you define what is going

